# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local
.playwright-cli/

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# Local Godot desktop test builds (mobile Web build under output/web is committed)
/output/linux/

# Godot export build artifacts (web build itself is tracked under output/web)
/output/*.zip
/output/linux/

# Precompressed payload is generated in the Docker image build, never committed.
output/web/*.gz
output/web/*.br

# Boot-smoke report is a CI check result, not a gated artifact.
reports/web/

# Playwright run artifacts. web_boot_smoke.mjs writes these as diagnostics —
# its boot frame always, and every screen of the walk under --shots — and nothing
# reads them back, so they are not baselines. Tracking them meant every local
# smoke run dirtied the working tree. CI uploads what it needs as job artifacts.
output/playwright/

# Lesson contact sheets from godot/tools/capture_tutorials.sh -- a review aid,
# regenerated on demand, 120 PNGs per locale.
output/tutorial-captures/

# Python bytecode. The asset guard imports audit_pixel_art as a module, so every
# run of tools/check_assets.py writes a __pycache__ next to the tools and dirties
# the working tree. Nothing reads it back.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Level contact sheets from godot/tools/level_walkthrough.mjs -- one PNG per
# screen-width of every level, ~190 images and 13MB per run. Same reasoning as
# output/playwright/ above: a review aid regenerated on demand, nothing reads it
# back, and the script overwrites the same filenames, so tracking it would put
# 13MB of binary churn in every commit that followed a capture run.
output/level-shots/

# Frames from godot/tools/focus_loss_repro.mjs. Same category as
# output/playwright/: a harness writes them on demand to show its own work, and
# nothing reads them back.
output/focus-repro/

# Frames from pin_entry_probe.mjs and touch_target_probe.mjs, same category.
output/pin-probe/
output/touch-probe/
output/pad-probe/

# SECRETS. Nothing in this repo needs a credential at runtime, and the one
# credential the project uses at all -- ELEVENLABS_API_KEY, for the offline
# sound generator in tools/ -- belongs in a shell or in a file that is never
# committed. Listed explicitly rather than trusted to habit: a key pushed once is
# a key that has to be rotated, and the web build is public bytes.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# ElevenLabs takes from tools/gen_audio_elevenlabs.mjs. Deliberately NOT assets:
# generation is cheap and wrong most of the time, so takes accumulate here and
# only the chosen one is promoted into godot/assets/audio (see the tool's
# --promote). Same category as the other output/ review aids above.
output/audio-takes/
